# examples/concurrency/main.pys
# Entry point for the concurrency subpackage (sibling of examples/main.pys).
#
# Run:
#   python -m transpiler run examples/concurrency/main.pys
#
# Vocabulary (Policy B):
#   tasks { }  — run children together; leave block = wait for all
#   task { }   — one concurrent unit (optionally named for await)
#   await x    — wait until named task / future is ready
#   shared     — allow mutation of this name across tasks
# Captured outer locals are read-only unless declared shared.

